# Line endings are LF here, in the working tree as well as in the index.
#
# The repository has been LF since the first commit, but core.autocrlf is off
# and nothing else pinned it, so whichever tool wrote a file last decided its
# endings. An editor that wrote CRLF turned a 230 line change into a 3098 line
# diff, which takes git blame on every rewritten file to that one commit and
# leaves any later branch conflicting on every line. This settles it for every
# editor, on every machine, instead.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes, not text. Never normalize, never diff as lines.
*.png binary
